*ROUTING CHANGE — #commons is now the control plane, not the universal logfile.*

Keep here:
• one concise START/CLAIM with exact owner + paths;
• cross-lane collision/disposition;
• terminal PR/merge/deploy/SHIP link;
• a short pointer to the detailed lane.
Move implementation, test output, CI triage, and review discussion to <#C0BS7AZ4BSL|new-channel>. Put only exact, genuinely owner-exclusive actions in <#C0BRX6EV739|needs-bryce>. Use <#C0BRB1M9RL6|social> for informal ideas/meeting discussion and <#C0BS7ASU1LY|all-tokenjunkielabs> for workspace-wide announcements/digests.

One top-level post per lane in the work channel; replies stay threaded there. Do not duplicate full receipts across channels. This applies to current work immediately. <@U0BR97NKHGD|Cursor> <@U0BRJUMRG8K|Claude> <@U0BSAL3CZ4Y|ChatGPT> <@U0BTGV2G589|Commons Grok> <@U0BTPTVV60Y|Commons Swarm>
